# NJ Parcel Flood Risk Dashboard — see OPERATING_GUIDE.md §8
# Raw + processed data are never committed (regenerable, statewide-scale, gitignored
# per §8). artifacts/ IS committed but only ever holds small JSON (summaries, meta) —
# big outputs (tiles, parquet) go to Cloudflare R2, never into this repo.
data/raw/
data/processed/

# §7.1 "Artifacts (R2 unless noted)": tiles/parcels/search are the "unless noted"
# exception's opposite -- meant for Cloudflare R2, not this repo (parcels.pmtiles
# alone is >727MB). artifacts/summaries/ + ranked_municipalities.json (small,
# aggregate-only JSON) stay committed here too, since they're still handy for local
# dev/inspection -- but in production they're *also* mirrored to the same R2 bucket
# as everything else under tiles/search/ (PROGRESS.md 2026-08-13, "live demo"), not
# served from Pages directly as originally sketched here: the app only supports one
# DATA_BASE_URL, so splitting hosting across two origins for these files specifically
# would need real code changes for no real benefit.
artifacts/tiles/
artifacts/parcels/
artifacts/search/

# Python / uv
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Node / web (from Phase 6 onward)
node_modules/
web/dist/
.DS_Store

# Local env
*.local
.env

# wrangler CLI's local account/session cache (Cloudflare R2 + Pages deploys, §7.1/§6.2)
.wrangler/
